ent Sep 1, LL-2025111) — a monthly subscription billing; Codeyard Team annual renewal Feb 14; Voltaro Energy payments.\n\nBut note: no debit alerts in October — the last was Sep 25, ~5 weeks ago. And no Ledgerline invoice for Oct 1 (the series stops at Sep 1 — interesting; maybe missed). Actually the Ledgerline series: Oct 1 2025, Nov 1, Dec 1, Jan 1, Feb 1, Mar 1, Apr 1, May 1, Jun 1, Jul 1, Aug 1, Sep 1 2026. No Oct 1 2026 invoice. So the monthly subscription invoice is missing for October — potentially notable! That could mean it didn''t bill, or the email isn''t there.\n\nI should mention the caveat: I can only see what lands in email; no direct bank feed, and no debit alerts at all in October — the latest is Sep 25.\n\nLet me present concisely with the headline. Also note amounts and that these are all in ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\nAlso note: the debited emails don''t say merchant (snippet empty, subject only amount). Could read one to get merchant details. The user asks \"any money moving out lately\" — the answer is amounts. I might read the most recent debit email to get the payee detail, which would be much more useful. Let me do that — get Sep 25 email body.\n\nLet me fetch the Sep 25 debit email and maybe Sep 12. To give payee names. I''ll read Sep 25 body.\n\nActually reading a couple of them would give payee names. Let me get Sep 25 and Sep 12. But that adds a turn. The user asked a question; better to answer well. I''ll fetch the two most recent debit emails.\n\nHmm, but I should just answer. Yet payee detail matters a lot (\"money moving out\" — to whom?). Let me fetch Sep 25 and Sep 12 bodies in parallel.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The core is the Konkan Bank debit alerts. Most recent: Sep 25, 2026 — INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821. Next: Sep 12 INR 450. Aug 2 INR 2,760. Jun 8 INR 980. Apr 17 INR 6,300.\n\n\"Lately\" relative to Oct 29, 2026. Most recent debit alert is Sep 25 — a bit over a month ago. Nothing in October. So \"lately\" —