n they share, and names, sizes and contents matched across all of them.\n\n**What''s identical on all 7**\n- `welcome.txt` (182 bytes)\n- `Clients/` → **Aozora Ceramics**, **Kaltwasser GmbH**, **Saffron & Sage**\n- `Clients/Aozora Ceramics/` → `Proposal - signed.pdf` (789 B) + `Rebrand/`\n- `Finance/` → `2025/` → `Budget 2025.xlsx` (1,819 B), `expenses.tsv` (357 B), `invoices.csv` (440 B)\n- `Team/` → `新しいロゴ案.png`, `voice-memo.wav`, `brand-tokens.json`, `Meeting notes 2026-10-05.md` (574 B) + `website/`, `Offsite 2026/`\n\nByte sizes are equal everywhere, so this is replication, not just similar naming.\n\n**Two real differences**\n\n| Drive | Difference |\n|---|---|\n| **#3 — FTP `766b212a…`** (the folder-scoped one) | Only `Clients/` is exposed — no `Finance/`, no `Team/`, no `welcome.txt`. It''s a **permission scope**, not a different dataset; the `Clients/` contents match the others exactly. |\n| **#6 & #7 — S3** | Have an extra **`edge/`** folder (identical in both): `big/`, `bulk-2500/`, `case/`, `deep/`, `docs/`, `images/`, `mislabeled/`, `preview/`, `special/`, `unicode/`, `empty-folder/`, `folder-marker/`, plus `empty.txt` (0 B), `one-byte` (1 B), `no-content-type.bin` (4 KB). |\n\n**Caveat on the comparison:** I verified root, `Clients/`, `Finance/`, `Finance/2025/`, `Team/`, `Aozora Ceramics/` and `edge/`. I didn''t open the deepest leaves (`Kaltwasser GmbH/`, `Saffron & Sage/`, `Rebrand/`, `website/`, `Offsite 2026/`, and `edge/`''s subfolders) — but the pattern held everywhere I looked, including identical byte counts.\n\nAlso worth knowing: file **metadata** differs by connector (S3 and FTP report `mimeType: null`, FTP shows no timestamps), and the S3 copies carry a slightly earlier seed time (09:41:16 vs 09:41:42). That''s connector bookkeeping, not different files.\n\nGiven five full copies of the same tree, those extra FTP/S3 connections are likely duplicates. Want me to finish the leaf-by-leaf diff, or check whether any of these drives has been written to independently since they were seeded?"}','assistant','v2','2026-10-29T11:24:35.241Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
